\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces  a) Diameter against depth $z$, where the diameter is the difference between the leftmost and rightmost bees in a layer. b) Density $\rho $ against depth $z$, where each bee has a default mass of $g$ grams. c) Supported weight $W$ (sum of weight of current layer and all others below it) against layer mass $M$. d) Coefficient of best fit $a$ against count. e) Attachment number frequencies, where the attachment number is defined as the sum of the in-degree and out-degree. }}{11}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bee_count}{{4}{11}{a) Diameter against depth $z$, where the diameter is the difference between the leftmost and rightmost bees in a layer. b) Density $\rho $ against depth $z$, where each bee has a default mass of $g$ grams. c) Supported weight $W$ (sum of weight of current layer and all others below it) against layer mass $M$. d) Coefficient of best fit $a$ against count. e) Attachment number frequencies, where the attachment number is defined as the sum of the in-degree and out-degree}{figure.4}{}}
