\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces (a) and (b) illustrate the diameter and density curves respectively as we vary the crawl rate while keeping the climb rate $\beta $ at $\sfrac {2}{5}$ and the number of bees at $250$. Similarly, (c) and (d) are the corresponding curves as we vary the climb rate and maintain a crawl rate $\alpha $ at $\sfrac {2}{5}$. e) is a phase diagram representing the spectrum of morphologies as we vary both $\alpha $ and $\beta $ (containing $100$ bees). }}{13}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:crawl_climb}{{5}{13}{(a) and (b) illustrate the diameter and density curves respectively as we vary the crawl rate while keeping the climb rate $\beta $ at $\sfrac {2}{5}$ and the number of bees at $250$. Similarly, (c) and (d) are the corresponding curves as we vary the climb rate and maintain a crawl rate $\alpha $ at $\sfrac {2}{5}$. e) is a phase diagram representing the spectrum of morphologies as we vary both $\alpha $ and $\beta $ (containing $100$ bees)}{figure.5}{}}
